  "text": "What does it actually cost an Indian family to stay in America today? $100,000. That's the new price tag on a single H-1B petition. Add a $250 integrity fee per person, a 1% remittance tax and a quadrupled border fee. A Bay Area engineer with two dependents now pays over six figures, before even starting a green card. The government expects $29 billion from visa integrity fees alone, over 10 years. H-1B workers at India's top IT firms nearly halved, from 34,000 to 18,000. When the cost of staying outweighs the dream, Bangalore stops being the fallback, it becomes the plan.",
